WEBVTT

00:18.890 --> 00:20.640
<i>What is this place?</i>

00:24.940 --> 00:26.150
<i>What's going on all of a sudden?</i>

00:29.780 --> 00:31.820
<i>What's beginning?</i>

02:09.750 --> 02:12.420
SECOND SELECTION
FIRST STAGE

02:16.300 --> 02:17.930
<i>A 'Blue Lock Man'?</i>

02:18.010 --> 02:19.300
<i>A hologram?</i>

02:19.390 --> 02:21.430
<i>Do they want me to score?</i>

02:23.010 --> 02:25.100
<i>It's gradually shrinking.</i>

02:25.180 --> 02:26.770
<i>I see.</i>

02:26.850 --> 02:29.650
<i>This is penalty area training.</i>

02:29.730 --> 02:31.560
<i>Quickly grasp the situation,</i>

02:31.650 --> 02:34.320
<i>and as the area shrinks over time,</i>

02:34.400 --> 02:36.570
<i>I have to beat the goalkeeper</i>

02:38.780 --> 02:40.110
<i>and score!</i>

02:40.200 --> 02:41.870
<i>Nice, right in the top corner.</i>

02:41.950 --> 02:43.580
<i>Its trajectory is really good too.</i>

02:44.620 --> 02:47.200
Are you kidding? Did it just save that?

02:47.290 --> 02:49.330
<i>He's on a different level from high schoolers.</i>

02:49.420 --> 02:51.750
<i>Besides, how did a hologram touch the ball?</i>

02:51.830 --> 02:53.920
REMAINING TO COMPLETE THE STAGE

02:54.500 --> 02:55.670
<i>I see.</i>

02:55.750 --> 02:57.720
<i>If I surpass this Blue Lock Man</i>

02:57.800 --> 03:00.180
<i>and score 100 goals in 90 minutes, I win.</i>

03:00.970 --> 03:04.510
<i>My own battle where my ego in front of the goal is tested.</i>

03:06.930 --> 03:10.140
<i>I can't score by taking random shots.</i>

03:10.230 --> 03:13.730
<i>Those without an extraordinary weapon cannot complete this room.</i>

03:14.480 --> 03:16.030
Interesting.

03:16.110 --> 03:17.110
Let's do this.

03:18.360 --> 03:20.070
<i>Here it comes. The ball is on my left.</i>

03:20.950 --> 03:22.660
<i>The goal is on my right this time.</i>

03:23.240 --> 03:24.990
<i>Analyze the situation instantly!</i>

03:26.290 --> 03:27.330
<i>Feel the trajectory of the ball</i>

03:27.950 --> 03:29.370
<i>and its speed,</i>

03:30.580 --> 03:32.330
<i>run straight to where it will land,</i>

03:32.960 --> 03:36.130
<i>measure the distance between me and the goalkeeper,</i>

03:37.000 --> 03:38.210
<i>and hit it directly!</i>

03:43.930 --> 03:45.800
<i>Good, it's working.</i>

03:48.520 --> 03:51.230
<i>This training is incredible!</i>

03:51.810 --> 03:54.100
<i>Since it replicates momentary positions in front of the goal,</i>

03:54.690 --> 03:56.190
<i>I can't win unless I enhance the power of my weapon</i>

03:56.270 --> 03:58.730
<i>and improve my abilities.</i>

04:01.030 --> 04:02.950
<i>No problem. I can handle it.</i>

04:03.570 --> 04:05.030
<i>My weapon is working!</i>

04:10.700 --> 04:13.000
<i>Did the number of holograms increase?</i>

04:14.000 --> 04:15.250
<i>Of course it would.</i>

04:15.330 --> 04:18.670
<i>If it's simulating the front of the goal, it's normal to have defenders.</i>

04:18.750 --> 04:20.090
<i>There!</i>

04:21.010 --> 04:22.010
So tough!

04:22.880 --> 04:24.590
The difficulty level went up.

04:25.220 --> 04:28.640
<i>It's not working. I need to improve my accuracy.</i>

04:28.720 --> 04:31.680
<i>If I don't evolve, I can't pass this stage!</i>

04:33.190 --> 04:35.940
<i>Balls randomly launched from the walls and</i>

04:36.020 --> 04:38.570
<i>this room with high-resolution panels,</i>

04:39.286 --> 04:41.640
<i>by developing and improving the facilities</i>

04:41.690 --> 04:43.570
<i>that increase player quality in top clubs in Germany,</i>

04:43.650 --> 04:48.080
allows each player to develop their own individual skills.

04:48.160 --> 04:53.210
But the best is the AI hologram goalkeeper, the Blue Lock Man system,

04:53.290 --> 04:57.210
created from data collected from the best goalkeepers.

04:57.790 --> 05:00.170
<i>By attaching a microchip to the ball</i>

05:00.250 --> 05:03.840
<i>and enabling contact with the hologram,</i>

05:03.920 --> 05:06.680
<i>Holographic sports technology.</i>

05:07.390 --> 05:10.180
I'll cut it short, Ego-san.

05:11.060 --> 05:13.140
We have no budget left.

05:13.230 --> 05:15.390
Shut up, Anri-chan.

05:15.480 --> 05:18.860
This is exactly what I envisioned.

05:18.940 --> 05:21.150
The way to complete this stage

05:21.230 --> 05:24.190
differs according to each one's talent.

05:25.150 --> 05:28.320
Those who have relied on others until now

05:28.410 --> 05:30.780
will struggle a lot in these 90 minutes.

05:31.580 --> 05:37.080
But for forwards who can make one from zero and are aware of their weapon, this is

05:37.170 --> 05:41.880
<i>an opportunity to develop their abilities and evolve.</i>

05:41.960 --> 05:46.590
Learn how to use your weapon and feel yourself improving.

05:47.180 --> 05:49.140
<i>When you leave this room,</i>

05:49.220 --> 05:52.220
<i>you will be on a completely different level.</i>

05:52.310 --> 05:53.310
That's it!

05:54.600 --> 05:56.730
<i>Three randomly appearing dummies.</i>

05:57.310 --> 06:00.610
<i>The direction of the ball, its speed, and finally the goalkeeper's position.</i>

06:00.690 --> 06:02.110
<i>If I can grasp all of this,</i>

06:03.440 --> 06:04.650
<i>I can score!</i>

06:05.360 --> 06:06.400
REMAINING TO COMPLETE THE STAGE

06:06.490 --> 06:10.530
It seems like the players who are evolving are scoring goals faster.

06:10.620 --> 06:13.410
This training is amazing.

06:13.490 --> 06:15.950
You haven't seen anything yet, Anri-chan.

06:16.040 --> 06:18.460
The fun is just beginning.

06:22.040 --> 06:25.420
REMAINING TO COMPLETE THE STAGE

06:26.010 --> 06:28.180
<i>'Final Level'?</i>

06:30.720 --> 06:32.220
<i>I have to stay calm.</i>

06:32.300 --> 06:34.180
<i>What I need to do should be the same.</i>

06:36.560 --> 06:39.140
<i>So fast! And it's coming with a spin!</i>

06:39.230 --> 06:41.110
<i>It's really hard to hit!</i>

06:43.150 --> 06:45.280
<i>Is this the 'final level'?</i>

06:45.360 --> 06:48.610
Balls coming at you as if in a real match,

06:48.700 --> 06:50.490
and randomly moving dummies.

06:50.570 --> 06:52.780
This is a simulation that mimics the front of the goal

06:52.870 --> 06:55.240
in a global-level match.

06:55.330 --> 06:57.580
Analyzing the situation and reacting,

06:57.660 --> 06:59.410
the accuracy and quality of the shot,

06:59.500 --> 07:02.580
and the endurance to do this for 90 minutes.

07:02.670 --> 07:07.050
Unless they are superior in every sense, they cannot complete this stage.

07:07.130 --> 07:10.720
<i>Fake forwards will realize their weakness here.</i>

07:11.390 --> 07:14.140
<i>Shit. I can't even score one.</i>

07:14.850 --> 07:18.060
<i>But I'm sure what allowed me to still run</i>

07:18.810 --> 07:21.480
<i>was that training.</i>

07:21.560 --> 07:25.440
<i>But in the end, I realized this.</i>

07:25.520 --> 07:30.360
<i>The reason I could score every time was because of Bachira's passes.</i>

07:32.740 --> 07:35.660
<i>Rather than irregular balls like this, he</i>

07:35.740 --> 07:39.120
<i>would send them exactly where and how I wanted.</i>

07:39.710 --> 07:43.580
<i>Kunigami would block defenders every time, and</i>

07:43.670 --> 07:47.550
<i>Chigiri would wait for a pass from me within my field of vision every time.</i>

07:48.260 --> 07:52.010
<i>I was able to score thanks to them.</i>

07:52.680 --> 07:54.930
<i>I had never fought alone until now.</i>

07:56.760 --> 07:58.270
<i>But this won't do.</i>

08:00.270 --> 08:02.900
<i>I want the strength to fight alone!</i>

08:03.770 --> 08:05.400
<i>I have to use all my abilities</i>

08:05.480 --> 08:07.440
<i>and do what needs to be done.</i>

08:07.520 --> 08:10.400
<i>I'll give it my all! Bring it on!</i>

08:11.610 --> 08:14.070
<i>Analyze the situation instantly!</i>

08:14.160 --> 08:16.410
<i>Read the positions of the goalkeeper and defenders,</i>

08:16.490 --> 08:18.870
<i>and run to that zone.</i>

08:18.950 --> 08:21.080
<i>According to the ball's trajectory and spin,</i>

08:21.160 --> 08:23.540
<i>shoot it to the top left corner!</i>

08:25.790 --> 08:26.790
<i>Not working.</i>

08:26.840 --> 08:29.250
<i>Even though my spatial awareness and positioning are perfect,</i>

08:29.340 --> 08:32.380
<i>I can't execute the direct shot I have in my head.</i>

08:32.470 --> 08:33.970
Damn it.

08:34.050 --> 08:36.510
<i>I can't get anywhere with the same mindset.</i>

08:36.600 --> 08:39.600
<i>What I need is to improve my first touch.</i>

08:40.810 --> 08:43.730
<i>First touches were easy with Bachira's passes, but</i>

08:43.810 --> 08:47.610
<i>interacting with the balls here is quite difficult.</i>

08:48.320 --> 08:49.480
<i>I see.</i>

08:49.570 --> 08:51.570
<i>I don't need to just lean into it.</i>

08:52.150 --> 08:53.900
<i>The power I use when shooting,</i>

08:53.990 --> 08:57.120
<i>80% of what it has been until now, no, 70% is enough.</i>

08:57.660 --> 09:00.330
<i>At the last second, I'll focus all my attention</i>

09:00.410 --> 09:01.830
<i>on the impact point!</i>

09:07.460 --> 09:08.380
That's it.

09:08.460 --> 09:10.550
This is my goal equation.

09:11.340 --> 09:12.970
<i>Every single direct shot</i>

09:13.050 --> 09:15.180
<i>has its own unique formula!</i>

09:15.680 --> 09:18.600
<i>Is this for real? It's incredibly fun!</i>

09:19.470 --> 09:22.220
<i>I'm discovering new things about myself every time!</i>

09:23.230 --> 09:26.100
That kid's shots have improved.

09:26.690 --> 09:29.610
Because humans are creatures that cannot learn without experiencing.

09:30.520 --> 09:35.990
When you learn your own limits, your perspective on everything changes.

09:36.780 --> 09:38.410
<i>That kid is now,</i>

09:38.490 --> 09:40.030
Yes!

09:40.120 --> 09:42.700
<i>terrified by his own evolution.</i>

09:42.790 --> 09:43.790
FIRST STAGE

09:47.000 --> 09:52.710
<i>I had never thought about my own goals in this much detail before.</i>

09:53.380 --> 09:55.590
<i>I can become even stronger!</i>

10:01.640 --> 10:04.560
<i>Is this the second stage?</i>

10:07.140 --> 10:09.730
<i>Teams of three?</i>

10:09.810 --> 10:10.976
FORM A TEAM OF THREE

10:20.030 --> 10:21.910
FORM A TEAM OF THREE

10:21.990 --> 10:24.040
<i>Nagi and Reo are here too.</i>

10:24.120 --> 10:29.120
<i>I see, since they need to be three, they're waiting for Zantetsu.</i>

10:29.210 --> 10:30.710
Ah, Isagi.

10:32.920 --> 10:33.920
Bachira!

10:35.960 --> 10:37.550
We met right away!

10:37.630 --> 10:39.760
Good job, congratulations.

10:40.550 --> 10:42.470
Hm, I see.

10:42.550 --> 10:46.020
So the second stage is just about forming a team?

10:46.680 --> 10:48.190
Who should our third be?

10:48.770 --> 10:51.270
Us two and one more person.

10:51.360 --> 10:55.530
<i>This guy just went and teamed up with me on a whim.</i>

10:55.610 --> 10:57.110
<i>It's no problem, but whatever.</i>

10:57.190 --> 10:58.700
<i>Who should we pick?</i>

10:59.280 --> 11:00.490
Let's see.

11:00.570 --> 11:03.410
If I think about our guys,

11:04.030 --> 11:05.910
<i>I can say Kunigami or Chigiri.</i>

11:06.910 --> 11:07.910
<i>Good idea.</i>

11:08.000 --> 11:11.880
But since we'll be three, we need to pick one.

11:11.960 --> 11:13.000
Who should we pick?

11:17.670 --> 11:20.760
How about teaming up with the first one who finishes?

11:20.840 --> 11:22.430
Why not?

11:22.510 --> 11:24.600
I guess this is our new team.

11:24.680 --> 11:25.680
Okay.

11:26.970 --> 11:28.770
Look, Isagi Yoichi.

11:29.413 --> 11:30.666
Will you team up with us?

11:32.060 --> 11:33.560
Join us.

11:34.150 --> 11:35.650
Hey, Nagi.

11:35.730 --> 11:38.280
Was he the one you wanted to team up with?

11:38.360 --> 11:39.530
Yes.

11:39.610 --> 11:42.610
Because he was the best player in that match.

11:43.450 --> 11:45.580
I want to play soccer with him.

11:47.120 --> 11:48.450
You heard him.

11:48.540 --> 11:50.620
What will you do? Are you going?

11:50.710 --> 11:52.670
Of course not.

11:52.750 --> 11:54.552
I'm teaming up with you, Bachira.

11:56.380 --> 11:57.880
Sorry, Nagi.

11:57.960 --> 11:59.550
But I can't join you alone.

11:59.630 --> 12:00.800
You heard him.

12:01.340 --> 12:02.340
I see.

12:02.840 --> 12:03.840
Then,

12:07.220 --> 12:08.930
I'll join you guys.

12:12.350 --> 12:13.750
That solves the problem, right?

12:14.560 --> 12:15.770
What...

12:16.270 --> 12:18.360
What are you talking about, Nagi?

12:18.440 --> 12:21.400
You <i>have</i> to team up with me.

12:21.490 --> 12:23.990
What is your goal? What about me?

12:26.530 --> 12:29.870
Reo, you taught me soccer.

12:31.040 --> 12:33.250
<i>We will become the best in the world.</i>

12:33.330 --> 12:34.460
<i>That's certain.</i>

12:35.710 --> 12:37.840
But we lost.

12:39.500 --> 12:41.210
We weren't the strongest.

12:42.840 --> 12:46.930
To understand this sadness I felt for the first time,

12:47.800 --> 12:49.890
I want to play soccer with him.

12:51.310 --> 12:53.600
I want to do my best.

13:03.360 --> 13:04.450
What's that about?

13:05.320 --> 13:06.450
Do whatever the hell you want.

13:08.370 --> 13:10.160
What should we do, Isagi?

13:11.540 --> 13:16.370
Teaming up with Kunigami or Chigiri would put my mind at ease.

13:16.460 --> 13:20.130
I know that's the best option. But...

13:23.380 --> 13:24.380
<i>But...</i>

13:26.800 --> 13:27.970
<i>I also, with this guy...</i>

13:30.510 --> 13:32.310
Join us, Nagi.

13:34.350 --> 13:35.350
Right?

13:39.309 --> 13:41.270
ISAGI YOICHI, BACHIRA MEGURU,
NAGI SEISHIRO

13:41.360 --> 13:43.150
ADVANCING TO THE THIRD STAGE

13:45.200 --> 13:48.820
See you later, Reo. I'll be waiting for you.

13:53.700 --> 13:55.870
Welcome, Nagicchi!

13:55.960 --> 13:57.330
Thanks.

13:57.420 --> 14:00.540
Reo looked a bit sad.

14:00.630 --> 14:03.090
Are you actually heartless?

14:03.170 --> 14:07.550
Huh? I'd be lying if I said I wasn't sad, but

14:08.340 --> 14:10.140
joining you guys is more exciting.

14:11.010 --> 14:13.770
Following my ego is the right thing, isn't it?

14:15.060 --> 14:17.480
This is what Blue Lock is about, right?

14:19.520 --> 14:24.030
<i>Right. This is a place where only egoists survive.</i>

14:24.820 --> 14:28.200
<i>If they're all true egoists, we'll meet again later.</i>

14:29.030 --> 14:30.030
<i>So for now...</i>

14:31.410 --> 14:33.290
Nagi, let's do this.

14:33.910 --> 14:35.410
Okay.

14:37.870 --> 14:40.710
<i>I don't think we'll lose with this trio!</i>

14:41.920 --> 14:44.750
Anyway, aren't we the strongest?

14:44.840 --> 14:46.210
Let's go.

14:46.840 --> 14:48.010
We'll definitely win!

15:02.730 --> 15:04.940
<i>Itoshi Rin?</i>

15:06.990 --> 15:10.200
<i>Greetings, rough diamonds.</i>

15:10.280 --> 15:13.166
<i>You are currently in the 3rd stage of the 2nd selection.</i>

15:13.246 --> 15:16.410
<i>3-on-3, team battle.</i>

15:16.490 --> 15:18.250
<i>Are we up against him right from the start?</i>

15:27.300 --> 15:28.170
Kunigami!

15:28.260 --> 15:29.260
Chigiri!

15:29.970 --> 15:31.720
Congrats on the first stage.

15:31.800 --> 15:35.220
You seem like the only one I know.

15:35.310 --> 15:39.520
I asked those guys over there, but they've already gone.

15:39.600 --> 15:42.940
The trio of Isagi, Bachira, and Nagi.

15:43.860 --> 15:45.360
Seriously?

15:45.440 --> 15:48.900
It's frustrating to be left behind.

15:48.990 --> 15:51.780
Yeah, I feel the same way.

15:52.990 --> 15:56.330
So, Kunigami, I have something in mind.

15:56.410 --> 16:00.830
We're probably thinking the same thing, Chigiri.

16:02.210 --> 16:03.443
-Let's team up.
-Let's team up.

16:06.250 --> 16:12.880
<i>The third stage is a battle in a mini-game format where 3-on-3 teams fight.</i>

16:12.970 --> 16:15.890
Both teams' goalkeepers will be a Blue Lock Man,

16:15.970 --> 16:18.930
and the first team to score 5 goals wins.

16:19.020 --> 16:21.310
The winning team

16:22.440 --> 16:26.230
takes one player they choose from the opposing team

16:26.310 --> 16:29.030
and forms a new 4-person team.

16:29.110 --> 16:31.490
Take a player?

16:31.570 --> 16:35.700
Oh, it's like that thing. You know that thing. That...

16:35.780 --> 16:36.910
Red Rover.

16:36.990 --> 16:38.200
Yeah, that one.

16:38.280 --> 16:41.960
<i>As you pass the stages, your teammates increase, and</i>

16:42.040 --> 16:45.830
<i>the team that reaches 5 people and reaches the 5th stage</i>

16:45.920 --> 16:47.920
<i>completes the second selection.</i>

16:48.000 --> 16:49.750
So what happens to the losers?

16:49.840 --> 16:53.220
<i>They return to the previous stage with the remaining players.</i>

16:53.300 --> 16:55.720
<i>If they also lose the 2-on-2 game,</i>

16:55.800 --> 16:59.810
<i>the unselected player is eliminated.</i>

17:01.350 --> 17:05.150
<i>This is everything about the second selection where you steal your opponents.</i>

17:05.230 --> 17:07.400
<i>The rivalry battle.</i>

17:07.480 --> 17:11.030
<i>You are free to choose which team you want to clash with.</i>

17:11.690 --> 17:14.610
<i>The match requires the approval of both teams to be played.</i>

17:14.700 --> 17:20.240
So those who form teams will keep coming here?

17:20.330 --> 17:21.580
I guess so.

17:22.370 --> 17:23.290
<i>In that case,</i>

17:23.370 --> 17:26.620
<i>we don't necessarily have to play against them.</i>

17:27.130 --> 17:29.750
If we get to take one player when we win,

17:29.840 --> 17:33.010
we don't have to play against players we don't want to take, right?

17:35.050 --> 17:36.590
<i>Exactly.</i>

17:36.673 --> 17:39.503
<i>Who you want to play against is the key to this stage.</i>

17:39.593 --> 17:41.153
<i>To help you decide,</i>

17:41.186 --> 17:44.390
<i>I'll announce the new Blue Lock rankings.</i>

17:46.480 --> 17:49.230
<i>Of course, there will be no deception this time.</i>

17:49.310 --> 17:51.070
<i>You are ranked according to</i>

17:51.150 --> 17:52.900
<i>the time it took you to complete the first stage.</i>

17:52.980 --> 17:58.620
<i>Everyone here is someone who could make one from zero on the field.</i>

17:59.320 --> 18:00.990
<i>This will be a battle where these 'ones' collide,</i>

18:01.080 --> 18:02.490
<i>mix together,</i>

18:02.580 --> 18:04.439
<i>and strengthen each other.</i>

18:05.750 --> 18:08.460
<i>Only those who can dominate the chemical reaction of egos</i>

18:08.540 --> 18:10.750
<i>will earn the right to advance to the next stage.</i>

18:11.380 --> 18:13.800
<i>Everything is fair to win.</i>

18:17.050 --> 18:21.430
<i>From now on, it's a battle where we'll steal our teammates and rivals.</i>

18:22.180 --> 18:25.100
He's set dirty rules again.

18:25.180 --> 18:28.980
In short, when we win and become 5, we complete the selection, right?

18:29.060 --> 18:30.190
Yeah.

18:30.270 --> 18:34.440
At least there's no rush to choose our opponent.

18:34.530 --> 18:36.240
What will you do, Isagi?

18:37.740 --> 18:40.450
<i>Should we wait for new opponents? Or...</i>

18:43.030 --> 18:45.870
What are we going to do?

18:47.620 --> 18:49.370
I don't want to do this.

18:50.880 --> 18:52.340
If we lose,

18:53.210 --> 18:55.170
nobody will pick me.

18:55.760 --> 18:57.550
And what if I lose after that too?

18:58.720 --> 19:00.760
Then I'll be left all alone!

19:00.840 --> 19:04.060
Enough! I don't want to do this!

19:04.640 --> 19:07.520
<i>What's with that guy with no self-confidence?</i>

19:07.600 --> 19:10.310
If we're going to play, let's play against those ranked 4th, 5th, and 6th.

19:10.400 --> 19:13.230
That would be the most glamorous.

19:13.310 --> 19:17.490
Winning against those tacky guys over there

19:17.570 --> 19:19.950
will never make me look good.

19:20.030 --> 19:22.990
Shut up. It doesn't matter who our opponent is.

19:23.950 --> 19:26.040
Let's just win quickly and advance.

19:26.870 --> 19:28.776
You two are just the fourth for a game of Okey.

19:31.000 --> 19:33.920
I admit that you are glamorous, but

19:34.000 --> 19:36.750
what are you aiming for by ignoring <i>'me'</i>?

19:36.840 --> 19:39.340
Hey, hey, hey! Please don't argue.

19:40.300 --> 19:42.010
<i>What kind of guys are these?</i>

19:42.090 --> 19:43.800
<i>Aren't they teammates?</i>

19:43.890 --> 19:44.970
What does 'glamorous' mean?

19:45.050 --> 19:46.760
He means 'eye-catching'.

19:47.350 --> 19:49.230
Don't get me wrong.

19:50.020 --> 19:55.110
We're just a team that came together because the three of us completed the stage quickly.

19:56.480 --> 19:58.570
You're nothing more than stepping stones to me.

19:59.240 --> 20:02.160
Both you and Blue Lock.

20:03.950 --> 20:07.200
If I win, I can enter the U-20 Japan National Team.

20:07.990 --> 20:12.040
I'm only here to take advantage of this system.

20:12.620 --> 20:15.250
All of this is to enter the Japan National Team

20:15.340 --> 20:16.960
and surpass my older brother.

20:17.710 --> 20:22.680
Crushing Itoshi Sae is my only goal in soccer.

20:22.760 --> 20:26.010
<i>I knew it. This guy is</i>

20:26.680 --> 20:30.430
<i>the younger brother of the genius midfielder Itoshi Sae.</i>

20:32.310 --> 20:34.730
How big is this guy's ego?

20:34.810 --> 20:38.690
That whole team is full of weird guys, don't you think?

20:39.610 --> 20:41.150
Even the way you were raised is glamorous.

20:41.820 --> 20:45.200
You're worthy of being my teammate.

20:46.320 --> 20:49.160
Being on the same team with such amazing people and all.

20:49.240 --> 20:51.660
I'll definitely be a burden.

20:53.870 --> 20:56.750
Bachira, Nagi. I'm sorry.

21:00.050 --> 21:03.170
<i>I know it's very risky, but...</i>

21:04.880 --> 21:06.640
It doesn't matter who it is, right?

21:09.060 --> 21:10.720
My ego

21:11.560 --> 21:12.930
is saying, 'Let's play.'

21:13.020 --> 21:14.690
<i>I want to clash against them!</i>

21:15.560 --> 21:17.190
That's the spirit!

21:17.270 --> 21:19.150
That was my plan too.

21:20.440 --> 21:23.030
Are you talking about <i>me</i>?

21:24.150 --> 21:25.740
<i>And most importantly,</i>

21:26.360 --> 21:28.660
Yes, it doesn't matter who it is.

21:30.120 --> 21:31.660
<i>I want him!</i>

23:06.550 --> 23:09.340
<i>Blue Lock, Extra Time.</i>

23:10.010 --> 23:11.800
Goodbye, big brother.

23:11.890 --> 23:13.510
This is as far as I go.

23:15.010 --> 23:18.480
When you become the best in the world,

23:18.560 --> 23:22.270
I'll appear on TV as your stunt double.

23:22.360 --> 23:26.360
I'm thinking of making my stage name 'Keisuke Davidson'.

23:26.440 --> 23:27.900
WANIMA JUNICHI

23:27.990 --> 23:29.700
Goodbye, big bro!

23:29.780 --> 23:31.820
Make sure you survive!

23:31.910 --> 23:33.570
ISAGI YOICHI
BACHIRA MEGURU

23:36.540 --> 23:38.080
Leave it to me, Keisuke.

23:38.700 --> 23:42.080
I'll destroy anyone who puts distance between us.

23:42.170 --> 23:44.540
I'm telling you.

23:44.630 --> 23:46.550
That just now...

23:46.630 --> 23:48.260
Wow, he can actually talk normally.

23:49.470 --> 23:50.420
<i>What a weirdo!</i>

23:50.510 --> 23:51.930
<i>Scary!</i>